[Event "Scandinavian: 3...Qa5"]

{The Scandinavian (1...d5) challenges e4 at once. Black accepts some loss of time with the queen for a clear, solid structure.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] The Scandinavian. Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. exd5 {Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
2... Qxd5 {Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
3. Nc3 {Gains time on the queen. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the queen on d5. That queen is currently undefended.}
3... Qa5 {[%cal Ga5c3] The queen pins the knight. Moves the queen out of attack to a5 and controls d5 and e5. White's last move put a knight on c3, which this now pressures.}
 (3... Qd6 {The modern retreat. The queen goes to d6 and controls e5, d5 and d4.}
4. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
4... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and d5.}
5. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
5... a6 {Stops Nb5. The pawn on a6 controls b5.}
6. g3 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
6... Bg4 {Develops the bishop to g4, where it controls f5 and e6.}
)
4. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
4... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and d5.}
5. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
5... c6 {Gives the queen d8 and stops Nb5. Supports the centre: the pawn on c6 controls b5 and d5.}
 (5... Bf5 {Develops the bishop before ...c6. The bishop on f5 controls e4.}
6. Bd2 {[%cal Gd2a5] Unpins, with Nd5 or Bc4 ideas against the queen.}
6... c6 {Now covers d5 and b5. Supports the centre: the pawn on c6 controls b5 and d5.}
)
6. Bc4 {Develops the bishop to c4, where it controls d5. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6... Bf5 {Develops outside the chain. The bishop on f5 controls e4.}
7. Bd2 {Unpins. Develops the bishop to d2, where it controls e3 and f4.}
7... e6 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls d5 and supports the bishop on f5. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nf3 & 3.d4"]

{White can delay Nc3.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... d5 {Scandinavian. Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. exd5 {Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
2... Qxd5 {Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
3. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
 (3. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the queen on d5.}
4. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
4... Bf5 {Develops the bishop to f5, where it controls e4.}
5. c4 {Gains time. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the queen on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
5... Qd8 {Safe retreat. The queen goes to d8 and controls d5 and eyes the pawn on d4.}
)
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the queen on d5.}
4. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
4... Bg4 {Pins. Develops the bishop to g4, where it controls f5 and e6.}
5. Be2 {Unpins. Develops the bishop to e2, where it controls d3 and supports the knight on f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5... e6 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the queen on d5. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls e5 and eyes the pawn on d4.}
7. c4 {Gains time. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the queen on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
7... Qh5 {Moves the queen out of attack to h5 and controls e5 and d5.} *
